    "slug": "doubly-linked-lists",
    "markdown": "# Doubly Linked Lists: Bidirectional Traversal & Node Deletions\n\nBy allocating a second pointer per node, linked lists gain the ability to traverse backward. This bidirectional reference structure is the **Doubly Linked List**.\n\nThis chapter explores **Doubly Linked Lists**. We focus on bidirectional node link structures, constant-time deletions, pointer safety, and memory trade-offs.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Bidirectional Pointers: Node Deletion Mechanics\n\nA doubly linked list node contains two pointer fields: `next` and `prev`. \n\n```cpp\nstruct DLNode {\n    int val;\n    DLNode* next;\n    DLNode* prev;\n    DLNode(int x) : val(x), next(nullptr), prev(nullptr) {}\n};\n```\n\nThis second link allows you to delete a node in true $O(1)$ constant time if you already hold a pointer to that node. Because you can access the predecessor node via `node->prev`, you do not need to walk the list from the head to find it.\n\n### Doubly Linked Node Linkage\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <rect width=\"600\" height=\"180\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#27272a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"35\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"13\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\">Doubly Linked Node Linkage</text>\n\n  <g transform=\"translate(45, 60)\">\n    {/* Node 1 */}\n    <g>\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"10\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <text x=\"15\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">null</text>\n      <text x=\"55\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">Val: 10</text>\n      <text x=\"95\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">0x6000</text>\n    </g>\n\n    {/* Links */}\n    <path d=\"M 105,22 L 175,22\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-double-forward)\"/>\n    <path d=\"M 175,38 L 115,38\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#eab308\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-double-backward)\"/>\n\n    {/* Node 2 */}\n    <g transform=\"translate(180, 0)\">\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"10\" width=\"110\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n      <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"10\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"50\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n      <text x=\"15\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#eab308\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">0x5000</text>\n      <text x=\"55\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">Val: 20</text>\n      <text x=\"95\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" font-size=\"7\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">null</text>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"arrow-double-forward\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"4\" markerHeight=\"4\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" />\n    </marker>\n    <marker id=\"arrow-double-backward\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"4\" markerHeight=\"4\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" fill=\"#eab308\" />\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n</svg>\n\n---\n\n## 2. Node Deletion Pointer Adjustments\n\nTo remove a target node from the middle of a doubly linked list:\n1. Set the predecessor node's `next` pointer to point to the target node's successor.\n2. Set the successor node's `prev` pointer to point to the target node's predecessor.\n3. Free the target node.\n\n### Doubly Linked Node Deletion\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n  <rect width=\"600\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#27272a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"35\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"13\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-weight=\"bold\">Doubly Linked Deletion Pointer Adjustments</text>\n\n  <g transform=\"translate(45, 60)\">\n    {/* Node A */}\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"10\" width=\"80\" height=\"40\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"40\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">Node A</text>\n\n    {/* Target Node (Bypassed) */}\n    <rect x=\"130\" y=\"30\" width=\"80\" height=\"40\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 1\"/>\n    <text x=\"170\" y=\"54\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">Target</text>\n\n    {/* Node C */}\n    <rect x=\"260\" y=\"10\" width=\"80\" height=\"40\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#111\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"300\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-family=\"monospace\">Node C</text>\n\n    {/* Rewired Forward Link */}\n    <path d=\"M 80,20 Q 170,-10 255,20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-dl-del)\"/>\n    \n    {/* Rewired Backward Link */}\n    <path d=\"M 260,40 Q 170,70 85,40\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-dl-del-prev)\"/>\n  </g>\n\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"arrow-dl-del\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"4\" markerHeight=\"4\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" fill=\"#10b981\" />\n    </marker>\n    <marker id=\"arrow-dl-del-prev\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"4\" markerHeight=\"4\" orient=\"auto\">\n      <path d=\"M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z\" fill=\"#10b981\" />\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n</svg>\n\n---\n\n## 3. Practice Checklist\n\n### Beginner Problems\n* [Design Linked List (LeetCode 707)](https://leetcode.com/problems/design-linked-list/): Build doubly list.\n  * *Why this is useful:* Build core bidirectional insertion/deletion pointer updates.\n* [Reverse a Doubly Linked List (HackerRank)](https://www.hackerrank.com/challenges/reverse-a-doubly-linked-list/problem): Pointer swaps.\n  * *Why this is useful:* Teaches you to reverse bidirectional chains in-place.\n\n### Intermediate Problems\n* [LRU Cache (LeetCode 146)](https://leetcode.com/problems/lru-cache/): Hash maps and doubly list nodes.\n  * *Why this is useful:* Combines constant-time hashing lookups with node splicing.\n* [Flatten a Multilevel Doubly Linked List (LeetCode 430)](https://leetcode.com/problems/flatten-a-multilevel-doubly-linked-list/): Flatten hierarchies.\n  * *Why this is useful:* Practices parsing list structures containing nested lists.\n",
